{"name":"Capri Fashion Pink","hex":"#ac839c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"capri","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep shade of sky blue between cyan and azure.","Used in capri pants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capri"},{"term":"fashion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A current (constantly changing) trend, favored for frivolous rather than practical, logical, or intellectual reasons.","Popular trends, especially in clothing; the industry that designs clothing and sometimes other related items."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make, build or construct, especially in a crude or improvised way.","To make in a standard manner; to work."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fashion"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Capri","blocks":[{"text":"Capri is an island located in the Tyrrhenian Sea off the Sorrento Peninsula, on the south side of the Gulf of Naples in the Campania region of Italy. A resort destination since the time of the Roman Republic, it is known for its natural beauty, historic sites, and tourism industry. It has 13,451 inhabitants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Capri_in_Cartolina_-_Vista_da_Termini_%28Massa_Lubrense%29.jpg/330px-Capri_in_Cartolina_-_Vista_da_Termini_%28Massa_Lubrense%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capri","wikidata":"Q173292"},{"title":"Fashion","blocks":[{"text":"Fashion is a term used interchangeably to describe the creation of clothing, footwear, accessories, cosmetics, and jewellery of different cultural aesthetics and their mix and match into outfits that depict distinctive ways of dressing as signifiers of social status, self-expression, and group belonging. As a multifaceted term, fashion describes an industry, designs, aesthetics, and trends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Carolina_Herrera_AW14_12.jpg/330px-Carolina_Herrera_AW14_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fashion","wikidata":"Q12684"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"},{"title":"Capri (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Capri or deep sky blue is a deep shade of sky blue which is the colour located halfway between cyan and azure on the colour wheel. It is a quaternary colour that has a hue of exactly 195 degrees on the RGB colour wheel. The complementary colour of capri is vermillion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Blue_Grotto%2C_Capri%2C_Italy.jpg/330px-Blue_Grotto%2C_Capri%2C_Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capri_(color)","wikidata":"Q19605446"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8_%D0%A0%D1%83%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%92%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8B_%D0%AE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B0.jpg/500px-%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8_%D0%A0%D1%83%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%92%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%BB%D